WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.067
(STAMMERS)

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.936
Um, sorry. Uh...

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:03.903
(YELPS)

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.504
(CHUCKLES) Sorry about this.

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:06.940
♪ (UPBEAT STRING MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:08.641
SPEAKER:
<i>He's not a natural showman.</i>

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:09.743
<i> He does get nervous.</i>

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:13.212
RICHARD BRANSON:<i> My mum tried
to get us over our shyness,</i>

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.380
<i> to challenge ourselves.</i>

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.851
EVE BRANSON:<i> We allowed them
to do a lot of dangerous things.</i>

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:21.221
<i> That's led onto
a few more daring things.</i>

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.190
VANESSA BRANSON:
<i> He thrives on jeopardy.</i>

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:26.825
It's a continuation
of his childhood.

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:28.794
RICHARD:
<i>Having suffered from dyslexia,</i>

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:30.663
<i>having left school at 15,</i>

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.165
<i> I had a lot to prove.</i>

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.433
SPEAKER:<i> He is a bundle
 of contradictions.</i>

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.036
SPEAKER 2:<i> People were seduced
 into thinking that</i>

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:39.238
<i>this was a bumbling, good guy,
 when, in fact,</i>

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:43.243
Richard always had a very
firm eye on the bottom line.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:46.245
RICHARD:<i> We had to use
 every trick in the book.</i>

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.982
SPEAKER 3:
<i>I don't believe that Virgin
could be what it is today</i>

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:51.850
<i> if he hadn't have done
 the boat crossings</i>

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:53.153
<i>and the balloon crossings.</i>

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:54.521
We're going to space.

00:00:55.921 --> 00:00:57.757
RICHARD:<i> Risk taking is a drug.</i>

00:00:59.191 --> 00:01:01.227
<i>A drug that started as a child</i>

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.398
<i>and has continued into my life
 ever since.</i>

00:01:06.365 --> 00:01:09.168
SPEAKER 2:<i> Richard was capable
of spending every single penny</i>

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.404
<i> on some project
that was gonna lose it all.</i>

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.240
VANESSA:<i> We've never
 taken it for granted,</i>

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.676
<i> that this can all
 just disappear.</i>

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.244
Poof.

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.180
♪ (MUSIC STOPS) ♪

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:25.184
RICHARD:<i> The spaceship's had
 a catastrophic failure.</i>

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:27.854
It's just ghastly all around.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.555
♪ (SOMBER MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.057
<i> If you've learnt the art
of trying the impossible,</i>

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:35.595
<i> you can turn that to
trying to do the impossible
 with anything.</i>

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:38.764
SPEAKER 4:
<i> That is the gift he has.</i>

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.501
RICHARD:<i> There is a danger that,
 by having that attitude,</i>

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.171
<i>that it could go horribly wrong.</i>

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:49.142
<i>I just feel that you should
throw yourself into life.</i>

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.278
<i> Life is short, anyway.</i>

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.548
<i>And I think it should be lived
 to its full.</i>

